Patchsu patch 2 of 2: local profiles (apply after 0001).

- Right-click your name in the top bar to switch between the online account and local profiles;
  left-click opens the local profile page (stats, PP graph, best/recent scores, editing in place).
- Local profiles send nothing to osu! servers, unless Settings -> Patchsu -> online lookups is on:
  then beatmap info/downloads, tags and leaderboards use the signed-in online account (scores are still never submitted).
- Per-profile play count, play time, hits, PP; optional Relax/Autopilot PP and count-all-as-ranked.
- Profile scores: click opens the results on top of song select at that map + difficulty (Esc returns there);
  right-click: view results, watch replay, show in song select, export replay, delete score.
- Plays already saved under a profile's name (online account, guest, older profile) can be synced to it
  (asked after creating/renaming; also on the profile chip's right-click menu): they are moved to the profile, and "unsync" gives them back.
- Settings -> Patchsu -> Patch 2. Local profiles: delete without asking (keeping / with scores), same-name sync suggestion on/off,
  and "create profiles with mod rules" (extra button in the profile page and switcher; opens mod select with "Profile rules":
  block / only allow / only allow with exact settings / select on switch).
- Profiles can be dragged into any order (profile page chips and switcher rows); trash button per profile in the switcher.
- Profile stats row laid out like the website (info left, grades right); scores follow Settings -> Gameplay -> Score display mode.
- Profile chips stay on one row (scrolls sideways, fades at the edges); compact "+ mods" button for profiles with mod rules.
- Mod rules picker: hides the profile page, behaves like song select's mod select (conflicting mods greyed out and unclickable),
  "Customise" on the left holds the profile rules, create button to its right. Mods a profile's rules don't allow are greyed out
  and unclickable in song select.
- "Transfer score" (under Export, on the song select leaderboard and the profile page) moves a score to another local profile in the database.
- "Only allow with exact settings": the profile's mod settings are put back whenever a play starts from song select.
- Renaming a profile / changing its flag updates its scores in the database; profile pictures show on leaderboards;
  clicking a local profile's picture opens its profile page (a note if it was deleted; guest plays do nothing).
- "Historical" on the profile page: Play History chart (months or weeks) and Most Played Beatmaps.
- An attempt counts as a play after 10 seconds, 30 judged objects or a 30 combo, whichever comes first.
- Local beatmap tags ("Local tags" in song select's beatmap details; searchable with tag="..."! or plain text), kept in patchsu-osu/.
- Auto-switch rules per profile (tags / star rating / BPM / length / mapper / name): selecting a matching beatmap in song select
  switches to that profile, and back again on beatmaps no profile wants.
- Auto-switching waits until a beatmap stays selected for 2 seconds; its notifications have a 3 second cooldown and can be
  turned off in Settings -> Patchsu. Lighter profile lookups for song select / leaderboards.
- Starting a beatmap always checks auto-switch rules first and switches immediately (profile, PP settings, mod rules),
  even when the beatmap was picked less than 2 seconds before starting it.
- "Total Accuracy" in the profile statistics: accuracy over every recorded judgement (all counted attempts, failed / quit too),
  next to "Hit Accuracy" (which only uses saved scores).
- Auto-switch rules can require selected mods ("Selected mods" button in the rules editor opens the mod rules picker):
  all of them / any of them / exactly this combination, optionally only with the exact settings. Changing mods re-checks the rules.
- Settings -> Patchsu: switch profiles on beatmap start, calculate and show total hit accuracy, count everything as ranked
  (every local profile), and do not hide unranked scores (best scores list shows scores without PP, faded and not weighted).
- Scores that give no PP on the profile are shown faded (their PP like an unranked play on the results screen), with the reason on hover.
- Profile page sections default to Scores first, then Historical (a dragged order is kept).
- Import replays (.osr) from a folder (subfolders included) as a local profile: Settings -> Patchsu (active profile) or the profile's
  right-click menu. Imported plays are synced to the profile ("unsync" gives them back); the .osr files are left untouched.
- Export a profile's top 50 replays (current mode, numbered by PP) or all its replays to a chosen folder: same two places.
- Settings -> Patchsu "Fetch top 200 plays of <profile> from osu!" (LocalProfileManager.BanchoImport.cs): the best plays (current mode)
  of the osu! player with the profile's name are added to the profile as plays without replays (no online ID, so the results
  screen never offers a replay that isn't there). Plays already there (same beatmap, within 2 s) are skipped. Beatmaps you don't
  have: a dialog asks, then they are downloaded (two at a time) and imported quietly under ONE progress notification that counts
  how many are downloaded and how many are left; each play is added as soon as its beatmap is in. Then the replays osu! has
  for the plays (that have none yet) are downloaded and imported the same way: the replay's score moves to the profile (synced,
  like imported replays) and the play without a replay is removed. Plays are matched by osu!'s score IDs, then beatmap + date.
  The notification can be swiped away (or clicked / closed) from the pop-up tray while it runs: that only moves it to the
  notification list (BanchoFetchNotification); closing it there cancels. Plays get ScoreInfo.BeatmapHash
  (a score only links to its beatmap while it matches); plays fetched before that was set are repaired on startup
  (LocalProfileManager.repairScoresWithoutBeatmapHash). Needs "Online lookups on local profiles": while it's off the button is
  greyed out but still clickable and leads to that setting. Also needs the online account signed in.
  Fetched plays count towards play count, hits and play time like synced plays (one play each, the map's length / rate as time):
  LocalProfile.BanchoScores lists the ones without a replay; ones fetched by older builds are marked once on startup
  (LocalProfileManager.migrateBanchoScores, profiles.json Version 2).
- Total Play Time is shown like the website / lazer: "5h 12m", "3d 4h 12m" from 24 hours on; the tooltip shows the total in hours
  (rounded), or in minutes under 2 hours.
- Settings -> Patchsu "Remove every play dated before the year 2000" (asks first): deletes local profiles' scores with broken dates
  (e.g. 1 January 0001) and forgets plays recorded on such days. Play History ignores such dates either way.
- Beatmaps whose difficulty can't be calculated are reported once (one notification) and never calculated again (no error popups);
  their scores can be removed from the notification or Settings -> Patchsu "Remove scores whose beatmap difficulty can't be calculated".
- "Exclude from PP" (every local profile): right-click a difficulty or beatmap set in song select, or a local score (song select
  leaderboard / profile page: this play, its difficulty or its whole set). Excluded plays stay in recent scores, play count and most played.
- Toolbar statistics update for local profiles: after a saved score, the profile button animates the PP and the estimated
  global rank (before -> change -> after), like lazer does for the online account after a score is processed. Deleting one of the
  active profile's scores or excluding / including plays, difficulties or beatmap sets from PP shows the PP lost or gained the same way.
- Fewer hint texts in Settings -> Patchsu; score rows show a coloured hover box (combo gold for a full combo, green with only slider ends missed; judgements; no-PP reason).
- The switcher's profile rows have the same right-click menu as the profile page.
- Profile pictures are stored at most 256 px (older ones are scaled down once) and decoded once for all avatars;
  song select skips the online beatmap lookup while the network is off (no blocked-request exceptions per beatmap change).
- Diagnostics: OSU_LOCAL_DISABLE=tags,autoswitch,... (or local-priority/osu-local-diagnose.sh / .cmd) turns Patchsu features
  off one by one at launch, to find which one costs performance.
- Profile page: statistics read only the needed values from the database; full scores / beatmaps are loaded only for shown rows,
  other profiles only compute their PP total, and results are kept until something changes (no rebuild flash).
- Profile page laid out like the regular player profile: compact header with cover toggle, rankings / small values / grades,
  profile chips in the buttons bar, info line, section tabs, Historical and Scores sections, website-style score rows.
- Failed and quit plays (once they count as a play) show in the profile's Recent Plays like on the website: rank F, no PP,
  not clickable, no right-click menu. They are kept in patchsu-osu/unfinished-plays.json (never in the score database)
  and forgotten after 24 hours.
- Profile score rows expand customised mods to show their value (e.g. "1.30x"), like the results screen.
- Settings -> Patchsu "Count LOCAL maps towards PP" (off by default): when off, plays on beatmaps marked LOCAL (changed in the editor)
  give no PP and are left out of profiles entirely (scores, recent plays, most played), whatever "Gray out scores..." says.
- Profile section tabs are slimmer, and the area behind the sections' rounded panels has the tabs' colour, like the website.
- Settings -> Patchsu (the tab and PatchSettingsSubsection come from 0001) has one "Patch N. ..." subsection per patch
  with settings, each in that patch's own file; the section finds them by reflection and sorts them by number, so
  patches never edit its list. 0002's own is "Patch 2. Local profiles"; its "Profile Colors" and "Online lookups"
  parts are LocalSettingsGroups headed by a plaque (the suggested-offset note style). The profile colour picker is
  LocalCompactColourPicker: hue/saturation square on the left, presets + hex code + page shades on the right.
- Settings (Patch 2's options and "Online lookups") are in the "LocalProfiles" section of PatchsuSettings.json (from 0001),
  not in profiles.json any more: older profiles.json files have them taken over once and removed. Everything else lives in
  <osu! data>/patchsu-osu/ (LocalProfileStore.DIRECTORY = PatchsuSettings.DIRECTORY; the folder used to be "osu-local").

